  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mirza Maheboob Baig S/O. Mirza Mohsin ... vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 January, 2019 Author: Mangesh S. Patil Bench: Mangesh S. Patil 1 20 ba 30.19.odt In The High Court Of Judicature At Bombay Bench At Aurangabad Bail Application No.30 Of 2019 Mirza Maheboob Baig S/O. Mirza Mohsin Baig Versus The State Of Maharashtra ... Advocate for Applicant : Mr. Ghatge Mahesh V.",
    "facts": "Alleging that a huge stock of scented tobacco was found in possession of the applicant during the raid effected on 28.10.2018 stocked in his godown the applicant was accosted. A report was lodged. The articles were seized. The crime was registered for the offences punishable under Section 188, 272, 273, 328 read with Section 34 of the I.P.C. and also for the offences punishable under Section 23, 26(2), 27, 30(2)(a) and 59(iv) of the Food Safety and Standard Act. The applicant was arrested on the same day and is now seeking bail after filing of the charge-sheet. 2. The learned advocate for the applicant submits that the Mirza Maheboob Baig S/O. Mirza Mohsin ... vs The State Of Maharashtra on 23 January, 2019 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/74668332/ 1 investigation is already over. Whatever muddemaal was found in possession of the applicant has already been seized. The rest of the offences are bailable. It is only the offence punishable under Section ::: Uploaded on - 24/01/2019 ::: Downloaded on - 25/01/2019 03:33:25 : 2 20 ba 30.19.od 328 of the I.P.C. which attracts severe punishment. However, there are no allegations constituting the ingredients for that offence. Therefore, the applicant may be released on bail. 3. The learned A.P.P. opposes the application.",
    "arguments": "As is pointed out by the learned advocate for the applicant, except the offence punishable under Section 328 of the I.P.C. the rest of the offences are bailable and do not attract severe punishment.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "As is pointed out by the learned advocate for the applicant, except the offence punishable under Section 328 of the I.P.C. the rest of the offences are bailable and do not attract severe punishment.",
